      "last7Days": "0.0",
      "projection": "Brazzell was selected by the Panthers in the third round of April's draft. He's expected to miss his rookie season due to a knee injury suffered in July. Brazzell is a tall, perimeter receiver with a big wingspan who will do most of his damage down field (career 14.2 aDOT at Tennessee) and doesn't offer much after the catch (3.6 RAC was worst in this rookie WR class). He has good speed (4.37 40-yard dash) and may settle in as a boom/bust low-volume, splash-play fantasy option. He'll battle for a starting role behind Tetairoa McMillan in 2027."
